{
  "requirement": "An operation MUST load user configuration only when its requirements call for\nuser settings. A missing user file MUST represent absent user configuration;\nwhether the operation can proceed MUST be defined by the feature. Loading MUST\nNOT create a file, repair malformed input, or supply an undocumented selection.\n\nWhen loading configuration, Habeas MUST report unreadable files, invalid TOML,\nunsupported user-file versions, unknown common keys, and invalid common field\ntypes. It MUST validate the feature sections used by that operation and report\ninvalid feature settings with the file and setting identified. Unknown keys in\nan explicitly documented provider-owned options map MUST follow that feature's\nvalidation rules.\n\nAn operation MUST NOT require or semantically validate configuration for a\nfeature it does not use. This isolation MUST NOT suppress TOML syntax errors in\na shared file that the operation otherwise needs to parse. In particular,\nordinary validation still requires a parseable `book.toml` while remaining\nindependent of authoring settings and the user configuration file. It MUST apply\nthe selected workspace's evidence path policy without loading its model clients\nor credentials.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The implementation covers essentially every obligation, and most have {test} references. The gaps are tests that verify parts of the requirement but carry no {test}`requirements.configuration.loading` reference. Both gaps were found by reading the test sources. I did not run the tests.\n\n**Obligations mapped to code and tests**\n- **Load user config only when called for; missing file is absent config; the feature defines whether to proceed.**\n  - Code: `resolve_authoring` and `load_user_config` in `src/config.rs`; `load_user_config` maps NotFound to `Ok(None)`. `main` in `src/main.rs` only loads workspace evidence settings, and only for commands that use them. `author_all_with_options` in `src/authoring/batch.rs` and `configured_assessment` in `src/authoring/mod.rs` decide when to resolve authoring config. `resolve_authoring_with_workspace_from` supplies the feature's \"no authoring configuration\" error.\n  - Tests: `absent_and_minimal_configuration_are_distinct_and_read_only`; `batch_fills_evidence_…` (an invalid or absent user file does not block a no-op batch); `ordinary_status_ignores_invalid_user_authoring_configuration`.\n- **Must not create a file or repair malformed input.** The loaders in `src/config.rs` only read files. `absent_and_minimal_…` asserts the file stays absent and unchanged. `unreadable_configuration_files_…` asserts that loading an absent workspace file leaves the directory empty.\n- **Must not supply an undocumented selection.**\n  - Code: `resolve_authoring_with_workspace_from` errors with \"no configuration selected\" or \"no authoring configuration\".\n  - Test: `configurations_without_any_selection_report_how_to_choose_one` in `tests/configuration.rs` verifies this, but it is tagged only `authoring.configuration_precedence`. This is the first gap.\n- **Report unreadable files, invalid TOML, unsupported versions, unknown common keys and invalid common field types.**\n  - Code: `load_user_config`, `workspace_document`, `parse_document`, `validate_workspace_common`, `decode`, `UserConfig::validate` and `WorkspaceConfig::validate`.\n  - Tests: `unreadable_configuration_files_…`, `invalid_schema_and_feature_values_…`, `workspace_diagnostics_identify_the_file_and_setting`, `explicit_credentials_round_trip_…` (malformed TOML through both the user and workspace parsers).\n- **Validate the feature sections the operation uses and identify the file and setting.** `BackendConfig::validate`, `UserAuthoringConfig::validate`, `EvidenceConfig::validate` and `invalid()` do this. Tests: `storage_rules_reject_each_invalid_field_with_its_setting`, `workspace_diagnostics_…`.\n- **Unknown keys in the provider-owned options map follow the feature's validation.** The options loop in `BackendConfig::validate` is tested by the option-key cases in `storage_rules_…` and `invalid_schema_…`.\n- **Must not require or validate configuration for an unused feature.** `load_workspace_evidence` decodes only `[evidence]`. Tests: `evidence_configuration_ignores_unused_authoring_settings_…`, `validation_checks_workspace_common_config_without_loading_unused_authoring_settings`, `status_loads_nearest_workspace_file_…`, `commands_without_evidence_inputs_ignore_an_invalid_workspace_file`.\n- **Isolation must not suppress TOML syntax errors in a shared file.** `workspace_document` calls `parse_document` and `validate_workspace_common` before any feature decoding. Tests: `workspace_diagnostics_…` and `validation_checks_workspace_common_config_…`, which check `version = [`.\n- **Ordinary validation requires a parseable `book.toml`, independent of authoring settings and the user file.**\n  - Code: `book_source_dir` in `src/evidence.rs` reports an unparseable `book.toml`; `inspect_repository` is independent of authoring settings and the user file.\n  - Tests: the tests that exercise an unparseable `book.toml` are `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` (`ci.book_source`) and `configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` (`ci.errors`), both in `src/evidence.rs`. Neither carries a loading `{test}` reference, and none of the loading-tagged tests cover the `book.toml` parse requirement. This is the second gap.\n- **Apply the workspace evidence path policy without loading model clients or credentials.** `PathPolicy::load` and `resolve_evidence_file` in `src/authoring/access.rs` call `load_workspace_evidence`, which never builds clients. Tests: `evidence_configuration_ignores_unused_authoring_settings_and_detects_credentials` and the evidence-path tests.\n\n**Gaps (unmarked tests)**\n1. `tests/configuration.rs` `configurations_without_any_selection_report_how_to_choose_one` verifies the \"no undocumented selection\" obligation. It has no `{test}` reference to `requirements.configuration.loading`.\n2. `src/evidence.rs` `book_source_defaults_only_when_absent_and_reports_invalid_configuration` and `configuration_and_dependency_failures_do_not_stop_later_checks` verify that an unparseable `book.toml` is reported. Neither has a `{test}` reference to `requirements.configuration.loading`.\n\nNo {fixme} acknowledges either gap.",
  "references": "18acef0d986e172dad2a8121eb997672f868e597e5814b14e914492321497586",
